1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,120
Once upon a time, there was a young woman.

2
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:12,400
The young woman was to marry a groom chosen by her parents,

3
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:15,720
and not her sweetheart, whom she loved.

4
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:20,120
She knew that her groom loved her very much,

5
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:24,260
but did her sweetheart care for her even more than that?

6
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:27,140
The young woman wasn't certain.

7
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:32,040
In the end, after wavering between the two of them,

8
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:37,720
the young woman even became unsure which one of them she really loved.

9
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:30,520
How long have I been searching for a way to return Mewtwo to the story?

10
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:34,520
All this time, I just took to hand whatever book struck me.

11
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:38,520
So why do I choose only books whose endings are missing?

12
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:40,520
Why?

13
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:44,520
What meaning is there to books with missing endings?

14
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:45,520
I...

15
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:47,520
Found you.

16
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:55,520
Geez, Duck, can't you go one day without getting stuck with cleaning?

17
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:57,520
Of course she can't.

18
00:02:57,520 --> 00:02:58,520
Sorry.

19
00:02:58,520 --> 00:02:59,520
Seriously, Duck.

20
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:00,520
No way!

21
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:01,520
What?

22
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:03,520
No, Duck, you mustn't look!

23
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:06,520
This is a shock.

24
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,520
Definitely.

25
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:08,520
Why'd you...

26
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,520
Oh, ow!

27
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:10,520
No, don't, Duck.

28
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:12,520
You mustn't look right there.

29
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:13,520
See?

30
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:15,520
Fuck here.

31
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:20,520
He smiled!

32
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:22,520
That totally ruins his bad boy appeal!

33
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:24,520
We're here to become a full-fledged elite!

34
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:25,520
Who is she?

35
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:27,520
Defending the bitingly sarcastic, fantastic Fakir!

36
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:28,520
Huh?

37
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:29,520
An older woman lover, huh?

38
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:31,520
We can't say that for certain yet!

39
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:32,520
That's right, Duck!

40
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:34,520
You should harbor unreasonable hopes!

41
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:35,520
Mind the truths!

42
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:36,520
Definitely break me!

43
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:37,520
Ahh!

44
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:39,520
My...

45
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:40,520
Huh?

46
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:41,520
Hey!

47
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:43,520
Oh, hey, Fakir!

48
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:44,520
Um...

49
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:45,520
Are you a friend of Fakir's?

50
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:46,520
Calling her just a friend?

51
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:48,520
That's some confidence she's got there!

52
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:49,520
Oh!

53
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,520
It's like I can see Duck's crying face before me!

54
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:53,520
I can't sit any longer!

55
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:57,520
We were all just on our way to the ice cream shop, right?

56
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:59,520
Um, they were just here.

57
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:00,520
You're an interesting person.

58
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:01,520
My name's Retzel.

59
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:02,520
What's yours?

60
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:03,520
Uh, mine's Duck.

61
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:05,520
Well, Miss Duck, Fakir and I are heading over to his house right now.

62
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:06,520
Would you like to come along?

63
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:07,520
What?

64
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:08,520
Retzel.

65
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:09,520
Why not?

66
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:10,520
Right?

67
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:11,520
Uh...

68
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:12,520
Uh...

69
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:13,520
Uh...

70
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:14,520
I'm impressed you found where I was.

71
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:15,520
You can't hide anything from me, Fakir.

72
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:16,520
Well, there's still...

73
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:17,520
Fakir, welcome home.

74
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:18,520
Hmm?

75
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:19,520
Hmm?

76
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:20,520
It's been a long time.

77
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:21,520
Uh, Retzel!

78
00:04:21,520 --> 00:04:22,520
May I come in?

79
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:23,520
Of course.

80
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:24,520
Who do you go well with, Zora?

81
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:25,520
It's a new lovey dovey, Zora!

82
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:26,520
Uh, is this your...

83
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:31,520
Last I saw you, Mewtwo and I just entered the Academy.

84
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:32,520
That's right.

85
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:33,520
I must admit, I was really lonely then.

86
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:34,520
Here you go.

87
00:04:34,520 --> 00:04:35,520
Thanks!

88
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:36,520
It's all right.

89
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:37,520
It's all right.

90
00:04:37,520 --> 00:04:38,520
Come here.

91
00:04:38,520 --> 00:04:39,520
Let's go.

92
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:40,520
Let's go.

93
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:41,520
Let's go.

94
00:04:41,520 --> 00:04:42,520
Let's go.

95
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:43,520
Let's go.

96
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:44,520
Let's go.

97
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:45,520
Let's go.

98
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:46,520
Let's go.

99
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:47,520
Oh, let's go.

100
00:04:47,520 --> 00:04:48,520
Let's go.

101
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:49,520
Let's go.

102
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:50,520
Let's go.

103
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:51,520
Let's go.

104
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:52,520
Let's go.

105
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:55,960
It's all right. I'm something of an older sister to Fakir.

106
00:04:56,260 --> 00:04:59,620
Really? I mean, no, I wasn't really saying...

107
00:04:59,620 --> 00:05:04,200
She's been like a mother ever since my parents died and I was taken in by Karan.

108
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:07,520
Sister's not lovey-dovey, Zura?

109
00:05:07,820 --> 00:05:10,120
Then is Retzel lovey-dovey was killed?

110
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:11,640
Now, now, Zura.

111
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:16,280
How flattering. We look that way. That certainly would be nice.

112
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:18,280
You shouldn't tease adults like that, you know.

113
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:19,980
You always treat me as a child.

114
00:05:19,980 --> 00:05:23,600
You know, I'm at an age where marrying someone wouldn't be odd.

115
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:27,440
Well, at my age, all you youngsters look the same.

116
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:30,580
I still see you as Fakir and Muto's playmate.

117
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,480
That's right. Where's Muto?

118
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:36,780
Oh, yeah. He's at school now. His dancing consumes him.

119
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:39,660
Aren't you always with him, saying I'll protect you, Muto?

120
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:43,700
And I will. You're staying here, right?

121
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:46,260
Actually, I plan to stay at the watermill.

122
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:47,560
I'll walk you there, then.

123
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:52,980
Thank you. But I think I want to take a little walk with Miss Duck.

124
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:53,700
Huh?

125
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:56,160
I'm a tiny bit jealous.

126
00:05:56,780 --> 00:05:58,580
Fakir with a girl as cute as you.

127
00:05:58,940 --> 00:06:00,640
Oh, no. I'm not cute at all.

128
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:02,900
The truth is, I'm always fighting with Fakir.

129
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:06,320
Actually, sometimes I just can't stand him, and you know...

130
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:10,720
I wonder if it's thanks to you that Fakir changed so much.

131
00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:11,780
Huh?

132
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:16,380
Say, is Fakir still writing stories?

133
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:18,280
Writing stories?

134
00:06:18,620 --> 00:06:20,940
The stories that boy used to write now and again.

135
00:06:22,080 --> 00:06:24,000
Sometimes they came true.

136
00:06:24,880 --> 00:06:25,500
What?

137
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:28,280
The stories he wrote actually came true?

138
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:31,700
He loved to write stories from the time he was very small.

139
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:35,020
They were just silly little stories.

140
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:38,320
But sometimes part of them would come true.

141
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:45,760
However, after he came to Kharon's house, he just stopped writing altogether.

142
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:48,040
Miss Retzel?

143
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:50,460
I've said a little too much.

144
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,460
I wonder if Fakir will scold me.

145
00:06:52,460 --> 00:06:57,380
To think Fakir wrote stories, and they came true.

146
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:00,460
If he can do that...

147
00:07:01,460 --> 00:07:02,460
Maybe...

148
00:07:05,140 --> 00:07:06,900
Miss Duck?

149
00:07:06,940 --> 00:07:09,560
Oh, sorry. I just remembered something.

150
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:12,060
Um, it was fun talking to you.

151
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:14,880
Fakir has changed.

152
00:07:15,480 --> 00:07:15,800
No.

153
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:18,460
The one who's changed the most...

154
00:07:20,080 --> 00:07:20,740
is me.

155
00:07:22,460 --> 00:07:23,360
Protect, huh?

156
00:07:24,780 --> 00:07:26,020
How do I protect him?

157
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,160
Who do I fight?

158
00:07:28,260 --> 00:07:29,780
You have to help me, Fakir.

159
00:07:30,180 --> 00:07:32,060
My heart, it feels so...

160
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:35,000
The story no longer has need of you.

161
00:07:35,860 --> 00:07:37,020
The fight has begun.

162
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:39,180
The story is moving.

163
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:41,880
Whether I'm here or not.

164
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:45,560
But all I have is a sword.

165
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:54,380
I'll protect Mewtwo with this sword.

166
00:07:56,380 --> 00:07:57,460
There you are.

167
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:00,440
Hey, Fakir, guess what Retzel told me.

168
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:03,400
She said stories you write have the power to come true.

169
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:05,480
She what?

170
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:07,020
If you really have that power,

171
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:09,560
and you write a story where Mewtwo gets saved in the end...

172
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:11,260
Fakir?

173
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:13,400
What are you saying?

174
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:14,000
Huh?

175
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:19,100
I said I heard some of the stories you wrote when you were little came true.

176
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:20,380
So...

177
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:21,140
Be quiet.

178
00:08:21,780 --> 00:08:23,160
But Mewtwo could...

179
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:24,020
Shut up!

180
00:08:24,380 --> 00:08:25,260
What do you mean?

181
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:27,360
Why are you talking to me that way?

182
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:28,160
Hey!

183
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:31,380
If I really could help Mewtwo by myself, Fakir,

184
00:08:31,540 --> 00:08:32,980
I wouldn't be asking you.

185
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:35,080
But right now, I can't do anything.

186
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:36,280
I said be quiet.

187
00:08:36,700 --> 00:08:39,220
I'll protect Mewtwo as a knight, end of story.

188
00:08:39,580 --> 00:08:40,960
I won't take orders from you.

189
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:44,080
Fakir, why?

190
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:45,520
Hey, listen to me!

191
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,940
Fakir, come on, Fakir.

192
00:08:47,940 --> 00:08:50,800
If you can help Mewtwo, then why won't you?

193
00:08:53,860 --> 00:08:55,020
What's with you two?

194
00:08:55,020 --> 00:08:58,480
We were waiting so we'd be ready when you came home crying.

195
00:08:58,480 --> 00:09:00,440
So, what happened with the wonderful Fakir?

196
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:01,840
I don't care what happened to him.

197
00:09:02,020 --> 00:09:03,020
Good, good.

198
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:05,680
Get mad and cry as much as you want.

199
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:08,480
And I thought we'd be able to help Mewtwo soon.

200
00:09:09,480 --> 00:09:09,960
Why?

201
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:22,380
He's kind of scared.

202
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:25,440
I'm getting shivers down my spine.

203
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:36,000
Retzel.

204
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:40,140
Mewtwo, I'm jealous of you.

205
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:41,020
Of me?

206
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:43,660
If I could live unchanging like you.

207
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:44,860
That's not how it is.

208
00:09:44,860 --> 00:09:48,420
See, I'm different than I was before.

209
00:09:48,980 --> 00:09:50,520
I've gotten my heart back.

210
00:09:50,940 --> 00:09:55,080
And that means now I can even accept your love for me.

211
00:09:56,580 --> 00:09:58,440
Now that's some happy news.

212
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:01,040
Maybe I'll call off the wedding then.

213
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:03,180
Wedding?

214
00:10:04,460 --> 00:10:07,380
That's Mr. Mewtwo, which means the girl is Miss Rue.

215
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:10,340
The two of them are getting married?

216
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:11,740
Is that right?

217
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:12,600
Getting married?

218
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:15,760
Students of mine getting married before my eyes?

219
00:10:15,900 --> 00:10:19,040
There is no happier, more joyful thing for a teacher than marriage!

220
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:20,440
Congratulations.

221
00:10:21,020 --> 00:10:21,640
Oh, thank you.

222
00:10:22,160 --> 00:10:23,400
You don't look very happy.

223
00:10:24,020 --> 00:10:25,240
Could it be you're wavering?

224
00:10:25,660 --> 00:10:26,920
Of course not.

225
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:29,200
I was only joking before.

226
00:10:29,380 --> 00:10:32,380
Hans loves me deeply from the bottom of his heart.

227
00:10:32,380 --> 00:10:35,620
With him, I'm sure I can have a happy life.

228
00:10:36,520 --> 00:10:37,340
Come now.

229
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:39,600
You can't lie to your own feelings, Ratzel.

230
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:42,920
You've got a pure and beautiful heart, haven't you?

231
00:10:44,420 --> 00:10:45,960
I'm going now, Mewtwo.

232
00:10:47,740 --> 00:10:50,340
I will have you love me and me alone.

233
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:52,920
Sacrifice your life and love me.

234
00:10:55,920 --> 00:11:00,000
If I do what Father says, someday he'll be my prince alone.

235
00:11:01,140 --> 00:11:02,100
Right, Father?

236
00:11:02,380 --> 00:11:08,800
The fight between the prince and the raven is being fought with fiercer and fiercer desperation.

237
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:11,940
In a place where no one can see.

238
00:11:11,940 --> 00:11:14,340
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha.

239
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:27,300
She's totally toying with him.

240
00:11:27,300 --> 00:11:28,240
That's right.

241
00:11:28,340 --> 00:11:33,300
A Fakir played thoroughly by an adult woman and then just tossed away like yesterday's newspaper.

242
00:11:33,660 --> 00:11:34,440
How wonderful.

243
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:38,120
Fakir said he would protect Mewtwo, so why?

244
00:11:38,820 --> 00:11:41,280
I'll protect Mewtwo as a knight, end of story.

245
00:11:41,620 --> 00:11:43,060
I won't take orders from you.

246
00:11:43,060 --> 00:11:47,820
And it was starting to look like we'd be able to work together, too.

247
00:11:48,540 --> 00:11:49,700
I don't like this.

248
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:52,740
No way I'll let it stay like this.

249
00:11:52,740 --> 00:11:53,780
Hey, wait!

250
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:56,200
Where are you going, Doug, for the second round, huh?

251
00:11:56,360 --> 00:11:58,960
That Doug really does love battles, doesn't she?

252
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:00,580
I see.

253
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:02,240
So Fakir said that.

254
00:12:02,740 --> 00:12:04,200
I want to help someone.

255
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:06,880
And he's someone important to Fakir, too.

256
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:12,040
So I thought if Fakir wrote a story, maybe we could help this person.

257
00:12:12,380 --> 00:12:13,340
But it looks like...

258
00:12:13,340 --> 00:12:13,940
I'm sorry.

259
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:17,020
This is because I've said something I shouldn't have.

260
00:12:17,220 --> 00:12:17,480
Huh?

261
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:18,660
Miss Doug, please.

262
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:21,740
Will you pretend that you never heard what I told you before?

263
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:24,960
But saving this guy will make Fakir happy, too.

264
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:28,200
In exchange, Fakir will end up hurt as well, though.

265
00:12:28,540 --> 00:12:28,840
What?

266
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:34,040
A long time ago, a lot of crows once showed up in Goldcrowned Town.

267
00:12:34,200 --> 00:12:34,720
Crows?

268
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:38,840
The crows attacked the townspeople indiscriminately.

269
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:43,560
Fakir was a child, but he must have wanted to do something to help.

270
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:47,600
He wrote a story where he became a hero and defeated the crows.

271
00:12:49,900 --> 00:12:54,340
And then, just like Fakir had written, the crows came and attacked him.

272
00:12:55,740 --> 00:12:58,340
But the ending was different than his story.

273
00:13:02,260 --> 00:13:05,340
